.TH sleep 1 (date) "GNU coreutils (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
sleep \- delay for a specified amount of time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sleep
\fI\,NUMBER\/\fR[\fI\,SUFFIX\/\fR]...
.br
.B sleep
\fI\,OPTION\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
Pause for NUMBER seconds, where NUMBER is an integer or floating\-point.
SUFFIX may be 's','m','h', or 'd', for seconds, minutes, hours, days.
With multiple arguments, pause for the sum of their values.
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/sleep#sleep--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/sleep#sleep--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
